1
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:34,990
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,789 --> 00:01:37,900
[Episode 6]

3
00:01:50,870 --> 00:01:51,590
Try it.

4
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:03,520
It's delicious.

5
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:04,930
You try some too.

6
00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:10,350
Why did you take the route in the letter?

7
00:02:11,610 --> 00:02:14,050
I thought I might run into you.

8
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:18,720
I figured the person you're looking for

9
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:21,140
would come to the place in the letter.

10
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:25,710
Why did you want to see me?

11
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:28,590
I'm working for Su Men,

12
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,370
Inspector Su, of No. 76 now.

13
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,280
I know.

14
00:02:39,870 --> 00:02:41,630
This is Shota Ishida.

15
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:46,240
He's Dr. Hoshino's assistant, I think.

16
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:51,840
The woman who corresponded
with your master before

17
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,770
is named Ouyang.

18
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:56,110
She used to be Hoshino's assistant too.

19
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:58,360
We previously wanted
to use Li Musheng's connections

20
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,280
to reach her.

21
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:00,960
But later, as you know,

22
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,000
we lost contact

23
00:03:02,470 --> 00:03:04,030
and haven't been able to do that.

24
00:03:04,030 --> 00:03:06,700
Didn't they have her address
for their correspondence?

25
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:08,230
All their previous letters

26
00:03:08,470 --> 00:03:11,240
were sent to the charity organization
where Ouyang was.

27
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,840
But she's not there anymore.

28
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:15,970
Her whereabouts are unknown.

29
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,480
You want to find Ouyang through Ishida?

30
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,400
Well...

31
00:03:24,770 --> 00:03:26,570
why are you looking for this Ouyang?

32
00:03:26,570 --> 00:03:27,470
This Dr. Hoshino—

33
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:28,800
what exactly does he do?

34
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:32,000
I see.

35
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:33,070
I won't ask.

36
00:03:34,030 --> 00:03:34,840
Don't worry.

37
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,000
I will find her.

38
00:03:36,030 --> 00:03:36,760
Definitely.

39
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:50,820
[Fairy Bath]

40
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:51,040
I want to learn from you.

41
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:53,630
Why the sudden change of mind?

42
00:03:54,490 --> 00:03:55,480
I want to have some skills

43
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,320
like you.

44
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:00,940
Then you have to call me master.

45
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,610
You haven't taught me anything yet,

46
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:05,610
and you already want to be my master?

47
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:06,870
Tell me first.

48
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:10,160
Are you with the Kuomintang
or the Communists?

49
00:04:21,410 --> 00:04:22,140
The Browning

50
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,720
M1910,

51
00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:25,040
known as the "Flower Mouth."

52
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,750
It holds six 9mm rounds

53
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:28,110
and weighs 1.2 catties.

54
00:04:28,830 --> 00:04:29,510
Lesson one:

55
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,100
Learn to protect yourself
with a gun.

56
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:35,520
You haven't told me yet.

57
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:38,430
Are you with the Kuomintang
or the Communists?

58
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:40,810
I need to know which sect I'm joining.

59
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,380
You don't need to know.

60
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:45,480
Just learn.

61
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:49,310
I guess you're with the Kuomintang.

62
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:52,850
Otherwise,
you wouldn't have killed Yu Yingxiang.

63
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:00,210
I told you not to worry about it.

64
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,190
Got it?

65
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,220
Within 10 seconds,

66
00:05:19,490 --> 00:05:20,690
put it back together.

67
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,360
What?

68
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,750
You can put a pocket watch back together.

69
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:28,430
A gun is nothing to you.

70
00:06:29,630 --> 00:06:31,430
I'm still not used to using a gun.

71
00:06:32,110 --> 00:06:34,920
Not everyone has to fight and kill, right?

72
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,250
I have a camera.

73
00:06:37,070 --> 00:06:39,390
Can you kill people with a camera?

74
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:42,170
A camera can record the truth.

75
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,860
It's more powerful than killing.

76
00:06:45,159 --> 00:06:46,070
Don't be silly.

77
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:50,050
Have you forgotten
how Cang Guanglian tortured you?

78
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:52,990
You can't even protect yourself
with a camera.

79
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,210
Remember,

80
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:10,410
only a gun can protect you.

81
00:07:22,310 --> 00:07:23,570
What's wrong with you?

82
00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:27,680
This is just the beginning.

83
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,380
I'll buy you a new one.

84
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:56,190
Aren't you in debt?

85
00:07:57,430 --> 00:07:58,140
Remember,

86
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:01,610
two things
are most important in these times.

87
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,600
Guns and money?

88
00:08:18,270 --> 00:08:19,160
Inspector Su.

89
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:22,430
You look relaxed.

90
00:08:23,810 --> 00:08:26,280
Business at the photo studio
isn't doing so well, huh?

91
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:28,720
I make more money working with you.

92
00:08:29,430 --> 00:08:30,890
It's just a bit dangerous.

93
00:08:32,789 --> 00:08:34,360
Today I'll take you to a place

94
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,620
that isn't dangerous.

95
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:36,549
Where to?

96
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:48,160
Are we taking fashion photos today?

97
00:08:48,870 --> 00:08:50,400
Stop talking and follow me.

98
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:58,670
[Big World]

99
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,080
Where are we?

100
00:09:31,680 --> 00:09:32,940
Far East Corporation.

101
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:35,710
Did you bring the photos
from the racecourse?

102
00:09:35,710 --> 00:09:37,040
Mr. Hoshino lives here.

103
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:38,970
He wants to see you in person

104
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,920
to thank you for saving his life.

105
00:09:40,950 --> 00:09:43,410
The Blind's prediction was quite accurate.

106
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,530
Who's the Blind?

107
00:09:58,150 --> 00:10:01,220
Thank you for your bravery, Mr. Chen.

108
00:10:01,630 --> 00:10:03,120
I admire it.

109
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,360
It was a matter of life and death.

110
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,160
Anyone would have done the same.

111
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:14,200
This toast

112
00:10:14,870 --> 00:10:16,150
is to Mr. Chen.

113
00:10:19,750 --> 00:10:20,440
Cheers.

114
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:34,330
Please have a seat.

115
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:37,710
Inspector Su,

116
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:42,590
your photographer
is as good-looking as you are.

117
00:10:43,910 --> 00:10:46,550
I didn't expect Chinese women

118
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,750
to be so beautiful

119
00:10:49,030 --> 00:10:51,150
and brave at the same time.

120
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:53,000
Very impressive.

121
00:10:53,830 --> 00:10:54,690
You flatter me.

122
00:10:58,070 --> 00:11:00,310
This is the unique

123
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:02,550
chivalry of the Chinese.

124
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:05,320
General, your understanding
of Chinese culture

125
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,720
is so thorough as always.

126
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:08,480
Chivalry?

127
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:09,910
What does it mean?

128
00:11:10,730 --> 00:11:11,380
General,

129
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:13,600
why don't you explain it?

130
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:17,510
I'm talking about broad-mindedness,

131
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:21,630
like the Shimizu Jirocho and his family.

132
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,970
Chen, where are the photos?

133
00:11:29,870 --> 00:11:30,790
Mr. Hoshino,

134
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,670
I brought you a small gift.

135
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Please accept it.

136
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:55,150
I will definitely treasure it.

137
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,150
Cheers.

138
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,030
Cheers.

139
00:12:02,510 --> 00:12:03,150
Cheers.

140
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:06,950
Cheers.

141
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:09,330
Cheers.

142
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:12,830
Cheers.

143
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:54,240
Director.

144
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:55,620
Are we leaving now?

145
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:21,660
I really miss it.

146
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:28,310
I saw you.

147
00:14:32,530 --> 00:14:33,530
Is this girl...

148
00:14:34,030 --> 00:14:35,720
also your assistant?

149
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,010
She has a very special aura.

150
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,530
You can notice her in the photo
at a glance.

151
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,340
Because she is a Chinese girl.

152
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:51,640
A beautiful Chinese girl.

153
00:14:53,270 --> 00:14:54,670
You guys look very close.

154
00:14:57,340 --> 00:14:58,550
I miss her,

155
00:14:59,930 --> 00:15:01,530
as well as the pan-fried buns

156
00:15:02,270 --> 00:15:03,230
and magnolias.

157
00:15:08,030 --> 00:15:10,230
She even treated you to pan-fried buns?

158
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:14,790
Yes.

159
00:15:16,870 --> 00:15:19,270
The best pan-fried buns
in all of Shanghai.

160
00:15:19,870 --> 00:15:20,510
Really?

161
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:22,790
Which restaurant?

162
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:23,850
I want to try it too.

163
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,160
Sorry.

164
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:30,060
There are many roads in Shanghai.

165
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:31,440
I can't remember.

166
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:34,630
I only remember

167
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:38,470
there were plane trees across the street.

168
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,390
In autumn,

169
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:42,720
fallen leaves covered the ground.

170
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:45,000
Under the sunlight,

171
00:15:45,290 --> 00:15:46,370
they were golden.

172
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:53,740
Very beautiful memories.

173
00:15:55,750 --> 00:15:56,560
Ishida.

174
00:15:56,850 --> 00:15:58,780
What are you doing? Come and drink.

175
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:03,200
What is this guy doing?

176
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,120
My favorite street

177
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:21,100
is Bubbling Well Road next to my house.

178
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:24,530
[Map of Shanghai]

179
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:23,360
Taking a tram from my house to the Bund

180
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:25,160
only takes less than 20 minutes.

181
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:27,760
For cakes, you have to go to Kaisiling.

182
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:39,910
Search one by one.

183
00:16:44,010 --> 00:16:45,870
The magnolia at my door has bloomed.

184
00:16:45,870 --> 00:16:47,200
Looking out the window,

185
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,330
I feel like I'm back in my student days.

186
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,720
This should be the place.

187
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
There are still people living here.

188
00:17:08,829 --> 00:17:09,480
Let's go.

189
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:11,589
Aren't we looking for Ouyang?

190
00:17:11,589 --> 00:17:12,849
Why aren't we going in?

191
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,440
We don't know the situation inside.

192
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,420
Then what do we do next?

193
00:17:19,550 --> 00:17:20,470
I'll handle it.

194
00:17:21,270 --> 00:17:22,599
You're ditching me again?

195
00:17:22,599 --> 00:17:24,060
What do you mean ditching?

196
00:17:24,069 --> 00:17:25,670
I just don't need you for now.

197
00:17:26,109 --> 00:17:26,750
I know.

198
00:17:27,150 --> 00:17:28,520
This is "killing the donkey after..."

199
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:29,780
"it has done the work."

200
00:17:31,350 --> 00:17:34,010
That metaphor doesn't seem
quite appropriate.

201
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:37,080
It's for your own good.

202
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:44,680
Let me go!

203
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:49,480
Chen Kailai, open the door!

204
00:17:49,790 --> 00:17:50,640
I'm here.

205
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,600
Where the hell have you been?

206
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,330
Where are your keys?

207
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:56,460
I lost them.

208
00:18:00,510 --> 00:18:01,160
Let's go.

209
00:18:02,630 --> 00:18:03,960
Where are you going now?

210
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:07,000
You run around every day
without making money.

211
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,530
I have to dance my heart out.

212
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:09,830
This family

213
00:18:10,070 --> 00:18:11,710
depends entirely on me.

214
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:15,280
Stop messing around
in the middle of the night.

215
00:18:16,030 --> 00:18:17,820
-What are you doing?
-Chen Kailai.

216
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:19,020
Today is my birthday.

217
00:18:19,510 --> 00:18:21,880
I really want to eat wontons.

218
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,830
You have over 300 birthdays.

219
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:27,340
You really are a very smart person.

220
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,470
My shoe fell off.

221
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:42,130
My other shoe is still outside.

222
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:48,400
Half-Immortal Hai, the fortune teller

223
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:50,370
from Zhugan Alley in Hangzhou,

224
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:53,410
said my Five Elements lack "Dong."

225
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,550
Your surname Chen has the character
"Dong" in it.

226
00:18:56,550 --> 00:18:57,920
So you are my man.

227
00:18:58,070 --> 00:19:00,070
Your grandma is Half-Immortal Hai?

228
00:19:00,270 --> 00:19:01,030
Besides,

229
00:19:01,550 --> 00:19:03,610
is there "Dong" in the Five Elements?

230
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:06,590
Can't there be "Dong"
in the Five Elements?

231
00:19:06,590 --> 00:19:07,650
Alright, there is.

232
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:11,630
I miss my grandma,

233
00:19:13,190 --> 00:19:14,120
and I miss my dad.

234
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:18,200
You can completely rest assured

235
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:21,190
about Yinbao and me.

236
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:30,700
Alright, go to sleep.

237
00:19:47,750 --> 00:19:49,270
Is she asleep, Mr. Chen?

238
00:20:15,010 --> 00:20:16,070
Young Master Feng!

239
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:22,790
There's nothing between Jinbao and me.

240
00:20:22,790 --> 00:20:23,520
Don't worry.

241
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,160
She is my boss

242
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:26,450
and my good bro.

243
00:20:27,360 --> 00:20:28,010
I see.

244
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:30,440
When do you

245
00:20:31,070 --> 00:20:32,590
plan to make her yours?

246
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:34,530
How could you say that?

247
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:37,230
These things take time.

248
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:38,790
You are always so passive.

249
00:20:38,790 --> 00:20:40,450
How long are you going to wait?

250
00:20:40,570 --> 00:20:42,550
Besides, she doesn't even like you yet.

251
00:20:42,550 --> 00:20:44,160
It's not that she doesn't like me at all.

252
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,000
Think about it,

253
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,270
she even remembers clearly

254
00:20:46,270 --> 00:20:47,400
that I love wontons.

255
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:48,030
Bro.

256
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,720
That's because she loves wontons herself.

257
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,980
She always lies to you.

258
00:20:52,410 --> 00:20:53,930
I won't allow you to talk about her
like that.

259
00:20:53,930 --> 00:20:54,990
Alright, alright.

260
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:58,750
Anyway, if you really like her,

261
00:20:59,070 --> 00:21:01,130
don't give up, and don't let her down.

262
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:03,220
You must make her happy

263
00:21:03,590 --> 00:21:04,920
and give her a warm home.

264
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,810
Well, I think in this world,

265
00:21:10,110 --> 00:21:12,190
only you can put up with her.

266
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:15,680
You really have patience, confidence,
and ambition.

267
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:17,600
She said

268
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:19,160
you are her cousin.

269
00:21:19,430 --> 00:21:20,600
As her cousin,

270
00:21:20,630 --> 00:21:22,830
how can you talk badly about her
like this?

271
00:21:22,830 --> 00:21:23,570
Her cousin?

272
00:21:27,990 --> 00:21:29,160
I'm her dad.

273
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:38,370
Hello, who are you looking for?

274
00:22:39,290 --> 00:22:40,540
I'm from the Ciji Foundation.

275
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:41,600
My surname is Shen.

276
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:43,990
Is Miss Ouyang here?

277
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:46,100
Please wait a moment.

278
00:22:55,430 --> 00:22:56,290
Please come in.

279
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,440
Hello, Miss Ouyang.

280
00:23:09,190 --> 00:23:10,780
Miss Shen, please sit.

281
00:23:13,310 --> 00:23:14,310
This way, please.

282
00:23:17,600 --> 00:23:20,800
I didn't expect the Ciji Foundation
to still remember me.

283
00:23:23,470 --> 00:23:24,330
Of course we do.

284
00:23:25,230 --> 00:23:27,490
You have donated to us many times before.

285
00:23:28,660 --> 00:23:30,690
But you haven't been there
for a long time,

286
00:23:30,690 --> 00:23:32,950
so the president asked me to come see you.

287
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:36,400
Indeed,

288
00:23:36,990 --> 00:23:39,190
I haven't contacted you for a long time.

289
00:23:40,930 --> 00:23:41,530
Thank you.

290
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:42,600
Please sit.

291
00:23:50,670 --> 00:23:53,270
Are you facing any difficulties,
Miss Ouyang?

292
00:23:53,830 --> 00:23:55,000
We can offer help.

293
00:23:55,830 --> 00:23:56,550
No,

294
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:59,110
I just went on a long trip.

295
00:24:02,030 --> 00:24:04,070
Go to my room and bring some pastries.

296
00:24:04,070 --> 00:24:04,750
Yes.

297
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:09,240
Have some tea.

298
00:24:17,270 --> 00:24:17,840
Come in.

299
00:24:22,750 --> 00:24:23,400
Director,

300
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:24,810
someone went to Lane 22.

301
00:24:26,310 --> 00:24:26,990
Who is it?

302
00:24:27,270 --> 00:24:28,030
A woman.

303
00:24:28,730 --> 00:24:31,530
The Ciji Foundation
is holding a charity auction.

304
00:24:32,110 --> 00:24:33,640
We would like to invite you.

305
00:24:34,100 --> 00:24:36,190
[Yukihiko, agent with No. 76]

306
00:24:36,720 --> 00:24:38,510
A phone call would have been fine.

307
00:24:38,510 --> 00:24:40,070
Why go through the trouble of coming here?

308
00:24:40,070 --> 00:24:41,000
It's no trouble.

309
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:43,420
It gave me a chance to come see you.

310
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:45,930
That's very thoughtful of you.

311
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:47,590
By the way,

312
00:24:47,930 --> 00:24:50,490
when did you join the Ciji Foundation?

313
00:24:57,230 --> 00:24:58,360
Section Chief Zhao.

314
00:24:59,530 --> 00:25:00,930
What kind of mission is it

315
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:02,820
that you need someone like me for?

316
00:25:03,220 --> 00:25:04,480
Catching Communists.

317
00:25:04,510 --> 00:25:05,710
We are short-handed.

318
00:25:06,750 --> 00:25:07,680
Please help out.

319
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:09,030
Thank you.

320
00:25:31,890 --> 00:25:34,680
Sorry, I really don't remember you.

321
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:37,030
When I arrived,

322
00:25:37,050 --> 00:25:39,110
you had already stopped going there.

323
00:25:49,640 --> 00:25:50,920
It's raining so hard outside.

324
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,180
Did you take a car here?

325
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:55,400
I took the tram.

326
00:25:56,350 --> 00:25:58,030
When the driver comes back later,

327
00:25:58,030 --> 00:25:59,400
I'll have him take you home.

328
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,600
Please don't bother.

329
00:26:00,730 --> 00:26:02,060
On the way here just now,

330
00:26:02,080 --> 00:26:03,540
I passed by Jing'an Temple

331
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:05,300
and saw several tailor shops.

332
00:26:05,550 --> 00:26:06,880
I'd like to look around.

333
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:10,000
Miss Ouyang,
do you have any tailors to recommend?

334
00:26:11,970 --> 00:26:13,830
It's hard for me to recommend any.

335
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:16,040
Miss Shen, you're so beautiful.

336
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:17,820
You'll look good in anything.

337
00:26:17,940 --> 00:26:19,380
My favorite street

338
00:26:19,410 --> 00:26:21,890
is Bubbling Well Road next to my house.

339
00:26:22,310 --> 00:26:23,310
I had a custom-made

340
00:26:23,310 --> 00:26:25,350
water-green silk qipao here,

341
00:26:25,530 --> 00:26:26,930
which is my favorite one.

342
00:26:27,860 --> 00:26:28,940
It's getting late.

343
00:26:30,670 --> 00:26:32,330
I won't bother you any longer.

344
00:26:34,090 --> 00:26:35,220
The rain is so heavy.

345
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:38,320
Why don't you wait until it lightens up
before leaving?

346
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:40,110
You can stay for dinner.

347
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:42,840
I'm not hungry.

348
00:26:43,270 --> 00:26:45,470
I had some pan-fried buns before I came.

349
00:26:46,070 --> 00:26:47,200
The one downstairs?

350
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,160
They looked good,

351
00:26:51,720 --> 00:26:52,770
but unfortunately,

352
00:26:52,770 --> 00:26:54,370
they didn't taste very good.

353
00:26:54,990 --> 00:26:55,750
Yeah.

354
00:26:55,960 --> 00:26:58,290
I don't think they taste very good either.

355
00:26:58,640 --> 00:27:01,640
The best pan-fried bun shop in Shanghai
is right here,

356
00:27:01,750 --> 00:27:04,080
simply because it's right at my doorstep.

357
00:27:05,750 --> 00:27:07,170
Let's get together another day

358
00:27:07,170 --> 00:27:08,900
and have something delicious.

359
00:27:34,510 --> 00:27:35,840
Please don't see me out.

360
00:27:37,070 --> 00:27:39,880
I have some things to donate
to the Ciji Foundation.

361
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:41,010
Wait for me a moment.

362
00:27:59,750 --> 00:28:00,730
I'll block the exit.

363
00:28:00,730 --> 00:28:01,250
Okay.

364
00:28:14,530 --> 00:28:16,260
Sir, your chestnuts are ready.

365
00:28:16,270 --> 00:28:17,270
What are you doing here?

366
00:28:17,270 --> 00:28:18,200
I'm buying chestnuts.

367
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:19,200
Are you guys going to arrest someone?

368
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:22,660
It's perfectly normal for No. 76
to arrest people in Shanghai.

369
00:28:25,070 --> 00:28:25,720
Stop!

370
00:28:56,430 --> 00:28:57,950
Zhao Qian, stop her!

371
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:20,790
You know I'm afraid of pain.

372
00:29:20,790 --> 00:29:21,860
Just kill me.

373
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:22,840
I will save you!

374
00:31:02,550 --> 00:31:03,240
Get out!

375
00:31:04,190 --> 00:31:04,920
Hurry up!

376
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:49,100
You've made a great contribution
this time.

377
00:31:49,100 --> 00:31:50,360
What I did was nothing.

378
00:31:50,590 --> 00:31:52,190
You were far-sighted enough

379
00:31:52,240 --> 00:31:53,160
to plan wisely

380
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:55,160
and prepare in advance.

381
00:31:55,550 --> 00:31:57,950
Go to the finance office
and get 800 yuan...

382
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:58,830
as a bonus.

383
00:31:59,880 --> 00:32:01,080
Thank you, Director.

384
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:05,120
Hello, Captain Cang.

385
00:32:11,590 --> 00:32:12,200
Director.

386
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:15,280
We have brought her
to the interrogation room.

387
00:32:22,550 --> 00:32:24,210
Ask Inspector Su to come over.

388
00:32:25,350 --> 00:32:26,880
And that photographer too.

389
00:32:27,060 --> 00:32:28,740
Why... Why ask him to come?

390
00:32:31,890 --> 00:32:32,440
Yes.

391
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:42,000
Tell me.

392
00:32:42,560 --> 00:32:43,880
Are you a Communist?

393
00:32:46,350 --> 00:32:47,110
I'm not.

394
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:50,250
I'm really not a Communist.

395
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:53,310
Then why did you run when you saw me?

396
00:32:53,440 --> 00:32:55,640
So many of you were chasing me with guns.

397
00:32:56,380 --> 00:32:57,110
I was scared.

398
00:32:57,550 --> 00:32:58,790
Of course I ran.

399
00:33:00,040 --> 00:33:01,570
Playing games with me, huh?

400
00:33:03,480 --> 00:33:04,590
It's a woman?

401
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:06,270
And quite young.

402
00:33:07,750 --> 00:33:09,590
They are used to disguising themselves.

403
00:33:09,590 --> 00:33:11,520
Don't be fooled by her appearance.

404
00:33:12,830 --> 00:33:13,920
How was she caught?

405
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:17,130
Section Chief Zhao caught her.

406
00:33:18,960 --> 00:33:21,200
Staying at the Logistics Section

407
00:33:21,200 --> 00:33:23,070
is a waste of his talent.

408
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:25,720
Looks like Section Chief Zhao is going to

409
00:33:25,720 --> 00:33:27,050
get a big commendation.

410
00:33:30,590 --> 00:33:31,390
Captain Cang.

411
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:33,820
We're counting on you now.

412
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:34,610
Understood.

413
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:43,640
I'll talk.

414
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:55,120
What?

415
00:33:56,510 --> 00:33:57,830
I... I'll talk.

416
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:00,030
Good.

417
00:34:01,060 --> 00:34:02,450
Are you a Communist?

418
00:34:07,650 --> 00:34:09,330
I... I am.

419
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:11,400
Why did you go to see Ouyang?

420
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:13,880
Do you have any accomplices?

421
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:16,580
I'm a volunteer for the Ciji Foundation.

422
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:18,630
I went to deliver an invitation to Ouyang.

423
00:34:18,630 --> 00:34:19,889
I have no accomplices.

424
00:34:19,960 --> 00:34:21,920
That's not right.

425
00:34:22,139 --> 00:34:23,540
I have no accomplices...

426
00:34:23,790 --> 00:34:24,460
I don't.

427
00:34:24,850 --> 00:34:25,639
I don't...

428
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:35,060
You'll have to confess in the end anyway.

429
00:34:36,030 --> 00:34:37,230
Why suffer?

430
00:34:37,230 --> 00:34:38,800
I'm telling the truth.

431
00:34:39,980 --> 00:34:41,389
I'm telling the truth.

432
00:34:42,510 --> 00:34:44,440
You're not telling the truth, huh?

433
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:48,760
I'm sorry then.

434
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:03,320
Do you smell it?

435
00:35:04,880 --> 00:35:05,590
What?

436
00:35:06,630 --> 00:35:08,030
The smell of a Communist.

437
00:35:10,860 --> 00:35:13,860
She will talk soon.

438
00:35:17,440 --> 00:35:19,040
You've already admitted it.

439
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:22,880
Why hold out, girl?

440
00:35:25,660 --> 00:35:27,030
You forced me.

441
00:35:29,450 --> 00:35:30,890
You forced me!

442
00:35:36,260 --> 00:35:38,790
Wasn't it the same
with Chen Kailai last time?

443
00:35:41,030 --> 00:35:42,320
No difference, right?

444
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:44,480
Just a forced confession.

445
00:35:47,710 --> 00:35:48,440
Director Li.

446
00:35:49,320 --> 00:35:50,380
You invited me here

447
00:35:50,670 --> 00:35:51,800
just to see this?

448
00:35:58,110 --> 00:35:59,280
Director, well...

449
00:36:04,590 --> 00:36:06,790
She delivered an invitation to Ouyang,

450
00:36:07,230 --> 00:36:08,480
and you arrested her.

451
00:36:10,550 --> 00:36:12,150
She didn't do anything else.

452
00:36:13,590 --> 00:36:14,440
Is that right?

453
00:36:15,230 --> 00:36:16,360
On the surface, yes.

454
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:18,800
But there's more to it.

455
00:36:21,390 --> 00:36:23,650
Interrogation is a time-consuming job.

456
00:36:24,350 --> 00:36:26,620
We can't jump to conclusions too early.

457
00:36:27,510 --> 00:36:29,110
As long as she is in our hands,

458
00:36:29,550 --> 00:36:32,080
we don't have to worry
that she won't confess.

459
00:36:32,590 --> 00:36:34,280
Who exactly is this Ouyang?

460
00:36:35,570 --> 00:36:37,630
Someone related to Project Slumber.

461
00:36:43,280 --> 00:36:46,540
How did you find out she was colluding
with the Communists?

462
00:36:48,110 --> 00:36:50,110
You'll have to ask Kagesa about that.

463
00:36:50,110 --> 00:36:51,510
I'm only responsible for catching people

464
00:36:51,510 --> 00:36:53,370
who have been in contact with her.

465
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:02,440
[Ouyang, Hoshino's assistant]

466
00:37:29,480 --> 00:37:31,460
[Musheng]

467
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:47,000
Who is Musheng?

468
00:37:53,890 --> 00:37:56,480
[Shanghai to Hangzhou]

469
00:37:55,900 --> 00:37:58,420
So you set a trap at her house

470
00:37:58,550 --> 00:38:00,750
to wait for people to walk right into it.

471
00:38:03,190 --> 00:38:04,000
Director Li,

472
00:38:04,670 --> 00:38:06,130
that's really brilliant.

473
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:12,590
What if that woman

474
00:38:12,590 --> 00:38:14,120
is really just a volunteer?

475
00:38:16,710 --> 00:38:18,630
Inspector Su, don't worry.

476
00:38:19,190 --> 00:38:20,720
Please trust my intuition.

477
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:04,280
I am truly innocent!

478
00:39:04,550 --> 00:39:06,610
You can't punish an innocent person!

479
00:39:18,260 --> 00:39:19,720
Did you take the pictures?

480
00:39:22,590 --> 00:39:24,150
I called you here to take pictures,

481
00:39:24,150 --> 00:39:26,190
to capture her most painful moments,

482
00:39:26,190 --> 00:39:27,990
not to stand there like an idiot!

483
00:39:29,070 --> 00:39:30,720
Do you even know how to take pictures?

484
00:39:30,720 --> 00:39:31,360
No.

485
00:39:34,550 --> 00:39:35,440
Are you scared?

486
00:39:38,490 --> 00:39:40,950
Now you know
how gentle I was with you before?

487
00:39:42,300 --> 00:39:43,190
Hurry up and take the pictures.

488
00:39:43,190 --> 00:39:43,960
I won't!

489
00:39:45,120 --> 00:39:46,290
Why are you yelling?

490
00:39:46,480 --> 00:39:48,550
Look at her! She's dying!

491
00:39:48,570 --> 00:39:49,970
Why are you so worked up?

492
00:39:50,510 --> 00:39:51,910
Because you wronged her.

493
00:39:52,870 --> 00:39:53,710
Look at her.

494
00:39:53,920 --> 00:39:54,880
So pitiful.

495
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:57,510
You wronged me like this back then too!

496
00:39:57,510 --> 00:39:59,910
Are you sympathizing with a Communist now?

497
00:39:59,920 --> 00:40:01,440
I'll tie you up right now! You believe me?

498
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:02,190
Do it!

499
00:40:02,190 --> 00:40:02,670
Bao!

500
00:40:02,670 --> 00:40:03,090
Come!

501
00:40:03,120 --> 00:40:03,880
Captain Cang is carrying out
the punishment!

502
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:05,740
Is it your place to point fingers?

503
00:40:06,070 --> 00:40:06,670
Leave here right now!

504
00:40:06,670 --> 00:40:07,800
-Tie me up!
-Get out!

505
00:40:08,630 --> 00:40:09,440
Don't make trouble here!

506
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:10,440
You're doing an innocent person wrong!

507
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:11,840
I'm pissed off too!

508
00:40:11,840 --> 00:40:12,480
Enough!

509
00:40:13,400 --> 00:40:14,400
Hurry up and get down to business.

510
00:40:14,400 --> 00:40:16,330
Don't let Inspector Su laugh at us.

511
00:40:19,670 --> 00:40:20,710
Wake her up!

512
00:40:20,840 --> 00:40:21,470
Yes!

513
00:41:01,920 --> 00:41:03,150
Next in Hangzhou,

514
00:41:04,070 --> 00:41:06,320
we need to pretend to be a couple
to cover our identities.

515
00:41:05,130 --> 00:41:06,960
[Five years ago]

516
00:41:07,030 --> 00:41:09,500
[Marriage Certificate]

517
00:41:08,280 --> 00:41:09,940
A pledge to grow old together,

518
00:41:10,190 --> 00:41:11,390
a vow of eternal love.

519
00:41:16,710 --> 00:41:17,800
Too bad it's fake.

520
00:41:23,070 --> 00:41:25,530
We don't need
to pledge to grow old together.

521
00:41:26,590 --> 00:41:29,390
I just hope
we can complete this mission together.

522
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:39,070
If I'm exposed,

523
00:41:41,590 --> 00:41:43,030
you must shoot me.

524
00:41:49,400 --> 00:41:50,730
I'm very afraid of pain.

525
00:41:51,550 --> 00:41:53,150
I don't want to give you away.

526
00:42:22,550 --> 00:42:24,530
You can't do this to an innocent person!

527
00:42:24,530 --> 00:42:25,820
I really know nothing!

528
00:42:43,000 --> 00:42:45,400
I told you
it's hard to survive in Shanghai.

529
00:42:45,960 --> 00:42:47,560
Working in a place like this,

530
00:42:49,590 --> 00:42:51,120
can you live with yourself?

531
00:42:56,630 --> 00:42:58,280
When I can't, I go to a certain place.
